            "review_title": "Review at Tian Long - Chaozhou Fresh Beef Hotpot",
            "review_text": "Jerry D\nHo Chi Minh City, Vietnam356 contributions\n0\nFirst time visit\nJan 2026 • Family\nLocated in the bottom level of Landmark 81. Family dinner to celebrate sons birthday. This is the closest thing I have come to in Vietnam that is similar to all the Hot Pots I visited for my Years in China. There was a small but nice selection of items to make up your dipping sauce. There were a few soup selections including 3 levels of spicy. We selected the first level because of my son but my wife and I agreed we could go a level up. The soup bowl is divided with a chicken broth on the other side.There were a various amounts of seafood, vegetables and beef on the menu. Wish they had included pork. The menu is on an Ipad and in different languages. The portions were fine. The staff was great.\nRead more\nWritten January 16, 2026",
